## 🔊 8. CENTRAL AUDIO ENGINE (`src/utils/audioEngine.js`)

* **Anti-Chaos:** `playSfx` / `playVoice` call `stopAllSFXAndVoices()` first (unless `stack: true`).
* **Buses:** `bgmGain`, `sfxGain`, `voiceGain` → analyser → master. Voices duck BGM.
* **Lip-sync:** `getLipAmplitude()` from analyser (or procedural chirp pulse when MP3 missing).
* **Fail-safe:** Missing `/public/audio/*.mp3` never crash React; `playVoiceOrChirp(name)` synthesizes a short talk chirp for demos.
* **Asset list** (exact filenames; see also `public/audio/README.txt`):

| Priority | Files |
| :--- | :--- |
| Voices | `voice_quest_intro`, `voice_no_nice_try`, `voice_tap_yay`, `voice_idle_1`, `voice_idle_2`, `voice_idle_3` |
| Cat | `sfx_cat_meow`, `sfx_cat_purr` |
| Core SFX | `sfx_wax_crack`, `sfx_wand_swish`, `sfx_spell_quest`, `bgm_intro` |
| Extras | `sfx_revelio_bell`, `sfx_chipmunk_giggle`, `sfx_peek_whoosh`, `sfx_footstep_soft`, `sfx_soft_chime` |

---

## 📦 9. 3D / GLB ASSET RULES (FOR CURSOR + HUMAN)

* Drop finals at: `public/models/minime.glb`, `public/models/ginger.glb` (see `public/models/README.txt`).
* Prefer single-file `.glb`, ~5–8 MB max for mobile.
* Prefer clip names: `Idle`, `Walk`, `Talk`, `Jump`, `Happy`, etc. — aliases live in `src/config/companionModels.js`.
* Never remove procedural fallback or CDN demo path without an explicit request.
* Always dispose Three.js resources on unmount (`threeDispose.js`).
* Visuals ship without audio; do not block UX on missing MP3s.

---

## 🧪 10. PREFERRED WORKFLOW NOTES

* Primary remote test path: GitHub → StackBlitz (user may skip local Node).
* When changing companions: update director poses + `clipAliases` + this blueprint together.
* Phase 2 WebAR hunt is still the largest unfinished production block; keep Screen 1–3 3D polish from regressing while building it.
